                <pb facs="1028" n="714" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg714"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111W74/5</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in France</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-20">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 20, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]</p>
                <p>Department has received following from President of Liberia:</p>
                <p>[Here follows the telegram of August 17 from President Howard.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1135-f1"/>]</p>
                <p>Inquire whether France has made such demands and, if the facts are as stated, you
                    may ask the French Government upon what grounds it bases the demands.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
